  "title": "The Placeholder King",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "creative-work struggles",
  "premise": "A designer wants to polish a title card but keeps treating a temporary gray rectangle as the final centerpiece. When the placeholder begins issuing absurd royal orders, the designer labels it TEMP, shrinks it to a corner, and finally draws the actual scene it was meant to support.",
  "hook": "The placeholder has taken over the project.",
  "visible_action": "Gray rectangle gains a paper crown; layout elements bow; TEMP stamp lands; rectangle shrinks; original scene expands behind it.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Make temporary decisions visibly temporary.",
